1
00:00:00,260 --> 00:00:03,120
Hi again. In this program, we've

2
00:00:03,120 --> 00:00:05,250
discussed that when you're
managing a project,

3
00:00:05,250 --> 00:00:06,675
you always have to consider

4
00:00:06,675 --> 00:00:10,740
the triple constraint:
time, scope, and budget.

5
00:00:10,740 --> 00:00:13,665
Each of these three elements
will impact the project,

6
00:00:13,665 --> 00:00:15,210
and if any one of them suffers,

7
00:00:15,210 --> 00:00:18,240
the overall quality of
the project suffers too.

8
00:00:18,240 --> 00:00:20,175
There's an important distinction

9
00:00:20,175 --> 00:00:22,455
between "quality" and "done."

10
00:00:22,455 --> 00:00:25,140
Simply finishing a
project isn't enough;

11
00:00:25,140 --> 00:00:27,390
the project must meet the
customer's standards of

12
00:00:27,390 --> 00:00:30,150
quality, rather than
just be completed.

13
00:00:30,150 --> 00:00:32,325
Like all things in
project management,

14
00:00:32,325 --> 00:00:35,010
the more effectively you
communicate with your team,

15
00:00:35,010 --> 00:00:36,300
the more likely your team

16
00:00:36,300 --> 00:00:38,855
will produce high-quality
deliverables.

17
00:00:38,855 --> 00:00:42,205
How do we define quality in
a project management sense?

18
00:00:42,205 --> 00:00:45,800
Quality is when you fulfill
the outlined requirements for

19
00:00:45,800 --> 00:00:47,600
the deliverable
and meet or exceed

20
00:00:47,600 --> 00:00:51,005
the needs or expectations
of your customers.

21
00:00:51,005 --> 00:00:52,715
When it comes to quality,

22
00:00:52,715 --> 00:00:54,410
it's important to
deliver a product or

23
00:00:54,410 --> 00:00:56,795
service that meets
your customer's needs.

24
00:00:56,795 --> 00:00:58,910
To meet their needs,
you have to know

25
00:00:58,910 --> 00:01:01,220
important quality
management concepts and

26
00:01:01,220 --> 00:01:03,230
oversee the implementation of

27
00:01:03,230 --> 00:01:05,750
a project management
quality plan.

28
00:01:05,750 --> 00:01:07,895
To set yourself up for success,

29
00:01:07,895 --> 00:01:10,654
you should consider
the four main concepts

30
00:01:10,654 --> 00:01:11,855
of quality management,

31
00:01:11,855 --> 00:01:13,910
which are: quality standards,

32
00:01:13,910 --> 00:01:18,800
quality planning, quality
assurance, and quality control.

33
00:01:18,800 --> 00:01:21,275
The quality process begins

34
00:01:21,275 --> 00:01:23,149
with setting quality standards.

35
00:01:23,149 --> 00:01:26,570
Quality standards provide
requirements, specifications,

36
00:01:26,570 --> 00:01:30,425
or guidelines that can be
used to ensure that products,

37
00:01:30,425 --> 00:01:32,300
processes, or services are

38
00:01:32,300 --> 00:01:35,030
fit for achieving
the desired outcome.

39
00:01:35,030 --> 00:01:37,430
Set quality standards
with your team and

40
00:01:37,430 --> 00:01:39,950
your customer at the
beginning of your project.

41
00:01:39,950 --> 00:01:41,390
Take the time to define

42
00:01:41,390 --> 00:01:43,895
the quality standards and
criteria for your current work

43
00:01:43,895 --> 00:01:45,800
so that your team
members and stakeholders

44
00:01:45,800 --> 00:01:49,025
understand exactly what they are.

45
00:01:49,025 --> 00:01:52,235
After you set those
well-defined quality standards,

46
00:01:52,235 --> 00:01:54,665
you'll want to check-in
periodically and make sure

47
00:01:54,665 --> 00:01:57,610
everything looks okay and
the requirements are met.

48
00:01:57,610 --> 00:01:59,930
Remember that well-defined
standards and

49
00:01:59,930 --> 00:02:03,775
requirements lead to less
rework and schedule delays.

50
00:02:03,775 --> 00:02:06,080
Let's put this in
an example using

51
00:02:06,080 --> 00:02:08,525
the scenario we've been using
throughout the program.

52
00:02:08,525 --> 00:02:10,790
You're a project manager
at Office Green,

53
00:02:10,790 --> 00:02:12,260
a company that specializes in

54
00:02:12,260 --> 00:02:15,155
plant decor for offices
and other businesses,

55
00:02:15,155 --> 00:02:18,160
and you're leading a
project called Plant Pals,

56
00:02:18,160 --> 00:02:19,910
a new service that will provide

57
00:02:19,910 --> 00:02:22,760
top clients with
desk-friendly plants.

58
00:02:22,760 --> 00:02:24,200
Here's an example of a few

59
00:02:24,200 --> 00:02:26,105
quality standards
for this project.

60
00:02:26,105 --> 00:02:27,965
Reliability standards:

61
00:02:27,965 --> 00:02:30,050
Each planter arrives by

62
00:02:30,050 --> 00:02:32,270
the agreed-upon time
and in good condition,

63
00:02:32,270 --> 00:02:33,935
ready to be placed at a desk.

64
00:02:33,935 --> 00:02:36,575
The suppliers have enough
plants in their warehouses

65
00:02:36,575 --> 00:02:39,600
to fulfill the customer
demand on time.

66
00:02:39,600 --> 00:02:41,340
Usability standards:

67
00:02:41,340 --> 00:02:42,970
Planters won't cause

68
00:02:42,970 --> 00:02:45,880
customers allergic
reactions or illness

69
00:02:45,880 --> 00:02:47,120
and will be suitable for

70
00:02:47,120 --> 00:02:49,570
all people and
animals, if necessary.

71
00:02:49,570 --> 00:02:52,400
Similarly, you may have
product standards:

72
00:02:52,400 --> 00:02:55,115
The supplier should meet
your brand's look and feel,

73
00:02:55,115 --> 00:02:57,080
use the specified materials,

74
00:02:57,080 --> 00:02:58,820
and be delivered intact.

75
00:02:58,820 --> 00:03:00,740
You should adhere to
quality standards

76
00:03:00,740 --> 00:03:03,290
across all products
and processes.

77
00:03:03,290 --> 00:03:05,030
For instance, you may have

78
00:03:05,030 --> 00:03:06,950
usability standards
implemented in

79
00:03:06,950 --> 00:03:09,170
the website development
process by stating

80
00:03:09,170 --> 00:03:11,555
that the website must
be easy to navigate,

81
00:03:11,555 --> 00:03:14,725
whether from a phone,
computer, or tablet.

82
00:03:14,725 --> 00:03:17,265
Next step, quality planning.

83
00:03:17,265 --> 00:03:20,780
Quality planning refers
specifically to the actions of

84
00:03:20,780 --> 00:03:23,930
a project manager or
the team to establish

85
00:03:23,930 --> 00:03:26,090
and conduct a process
for identifying and

86
00:03:26,090 --> 00:03:28,310
determining exactly
which standards of

87
00:03:28,310 --> 00:03:30,830
quality are in fact
relevant to the project as

88
00:03:30,830 --> 00:03:34,085
a whole, and how to satisfy them.

89
00:03:34,085 --> 00:03:35,960
To steer that discussion,

90
00:03:35,960 --> 00:03:37,270
you can ask yourself,

91
00:03:37,270 --> 00:03:38,840
"What outcome do my customers

92
00:03:38,840 --> 00:03:40,685
want at the end of this project?

93
00:03:40,685 --> 00:03:43,160
What does quality
look like for them?

94
00:03:43,160 --> 00:03:46,370
How can I meet
their expectations?

95
00:03:46,370 --> 00:03:48,170
How will I determine if

96
00:03:48,170 --> 00:03:51,220
the quality measures will
lead to project success?"

97
00:03:51,220 --> 00:03:53,509
This is where you'll
plan the procedures

98
00:03:53,509 --> 00:03:56,030
to achieve the quality standards.

99
00:03:56,030 --> 00:03:58,055
Recall that one of the Project

100
00:03:58,055 --> 00:03:59,540
Plant Pals quality standards

101
00:03:59,540 --> 00:04:01,135
is reliability,

102
00:04:01,135 --> 00:04:03,050
the expectation that each plant

103
00:04:03,050 --> 00:04:05,585
arrives on time and
in good condition.

104
00:04:05,585 --> 00:04:08,330
So as a quality planning measure,

105
00:04:08,330 --> 00:04:09,920
you'll need to make plans

106
00:04:09,920 --> 00:04:11,600
with your plant provider to test

107
00:04:11,600 --> 00:04:12,980
the durability of your planters

108
00:04:12,980 --> 00:04:15,280
before you decide to use them.

109
00:04:15,280 --> 00:04:16,700
The third concept of

110
00:04:16,700 --> 00:04:19,205
quality management is
quality assurance.

111
00:04:19,205 --> 00:04:22,235
Quality assurance,
often shortened to QA,

112
00:04:22,235 --> 00:04:25,250
is all about evaluating
if your project is moving

113
00:04:25,250 --> 00:04:28,535
towards delivering a high-quality
service or product.

114
00:04:28,535 --> 00:04:30,950
Unlike quality standards
and quality planning,

115
00:04:30,950 --> 00:04:33,585
QA spans the whole
project life cycle,

116
00:04:33,585 --> 00:04:36,395
rather than taking place
at a specific phase.

117
00:04:36,395 --> 00:04:38,810
Your quality plan should

118
00:04:38,810 --> 00:04:40,745
include regular audits to confirm

119
00:04:40,745 --> 00:04:42,440
that everything is
going to plan and

120
00:04:42,440 --> 00:04:45,215
the necessary procedures
are being followed.

121
00:04:45,215 --> 00:04:48,110
Regular check-ins and
reporting to stakeholders will

122
00:04:48,110 --> 00:04:51,240
help boost their confidence,
and yours, along the way.

123
00:04:51,240 --> 00:04:54,680
Quality assurance is where
you'll make sure that you and

124
00:04:54,680 --> 00:04:56,720
your clients are getting
the exact product

125
00:04:56,720 --> 00:04:58,085
you contracted for.

126
00:04:58,085 --> 00:04:59,915
So with Project Plant Pals,

127
00:04:59,915 --> 00:05:02,300
this is where your team
will inspect options for

128
00:05:02,300 --> 00:05:05,785
planters and perhaps sit in
on the durability testing.

129
00:05:05,785 --> 00:05:08,000
If you make plans for
your plant provider to

130
00:05:08,000 --> 00:05:10,535
handle the durability
testing on their own,

131
00:05:10,535 --> 00:05:12,050
make sure you are tracking

132
00:05:12,050 --> 00:05:14,480
their progress and
checking in regularly.

133
00:05:14,480 --> 00:05:15,980
The final concept of

134
00:05:15,980 --> 00:05:18,095
quality management
is quality control,

135
00:05:18,095 --> 00:05:20,030
often shortened to QC.

136
00:05:20,030 --> 00:05:22,370
Here, techniques are used in

137
00:05:22,370 --> 00:05:24,470
order to ensure
quality standards when

138
00:05:24,470 --> 00:05:26,510
a problem is identified, or if

139
00:05:26,510 --> 00:05:29,090
the quality plan is not
executed in the desired manner

140
00:05:29,090 --> 00:05:31,805
and corrective actions
should be affected.

141
00:05:31,805 --> 00:05:35,480
Quality control involves
monitoring project results and

142
00:05:35,480 --> 00:05:37,220
delivery to determine
if they are

143
00:05:37,220 --> 00:05:39,310
meeting desired results or not.

144
00:05:39,310 --> 00:05:43,145
If not, then alternative
actions should be taken.

145
00:05:43,145 --> 00:05:45,470
Quality control is
also integral to

146
00:05:45,470 --> 00:05:48,725
creating a more successful
landing for the next project.

147
00:05:48,725 --> 00:05:50,180
After the plants are placed

148
00:05:50,180 --> 00:05:51,860
throughout the
customers' offices,

149
00:05:51,860 --> 00:05:54,290
quality control may
look like you or

150
00:05:54,290 --> 00:05:56,000
your team member taking a final

151
00:05:56,000 --> 00:05:57,170
walk-through of the offices

152
00:05:57,170 --> 00:05:58,835
where the plants were delivered.

153
00:05:58,835 --> 00:06:00,560
You'd be checking for things like

154
00:06:00,560 --> 00:06:02,390
broken planters or plants

155
00:06:02,390 --> 00:06:03,875
that were damaged in transit

156
00:06:03,875 --> 00:06:05,764
and swapping them
out when necessary.

157
00:06:05,764 --> 00:06:08,195
You may not do this
for every customer,

158
00:06:08,195 --> 00:06:09,665
but it's a good idea to do it

159
00:06:09,665 --> 00:06:11,360
as you're starting
out in case you

160
00:06:11,360 --> 00:06:12,800
spot issues to improve

161
00:06:12,800 --> 00:06:14,915
upon when you're
back in the office.

162
00:06:14,915 --> 00:06:17,135
If you stuck to
your quality plan,

163
00:06:17,135 --> 00:06:18,560
checking on quality throughout

164
00:06:18,560 --> 00:06:20,060
the life cycle of your project

165
00:06:20,060 --> 00:06:23,225
(QA), and of course
correcting as needed (QC),

166
00:06:23,225 --> 00:06:25,520
the likelihood of meeting
your quality standards is

167
00:06:25,520 --> 00:06:27,830
high, resulting in a
high-quality deliverable at

168
00:06:27,830 --> 00:06:29,660
the end of your
project that satisfies

169
00:06:29,660 --> 00:06:31,280
your organizational goals and

170
00:06:31,280 --> 00:06:33,550
exceeds the customer's
expectations.

171
00:06:33,550 --> 00:06:36,225
And there you have it—quality
management!

172
00:06:36,225 --> 00:06:38,990
Great! So now we've learned
more about how to

173
00:06:38,990 --> 00:06:41,675
identify and explain the
concept of quality management,

174
00:06:41,675 --> 00:06:43,640
which includes quality standards,

175
00:06:43,640 --> 00:06:47,435
quality planning, quality
assurance, and quality control.

176
00:06:47,435 --> 00:06:49,910
In the next video,
we'll discuss how

177
00:06:49,910 --> 00:06:51,980
to use soft skills,
like negotiating and

178
00:06:51,980 --> 00:06:53,330
practicing empathy, to meet

179
00:06:53,330 --> 00:06:57,360
customers' needs in terms
of quality. Meet you there!
